<article class="env-lemma" id="02MC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02MC">Lemma <span data-tag="02MC">10.121.1</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a semi-local Noetherian ring of dimension $1$. If $a, b \in R$ are nonzerodivisors then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{length}_ R(R/(ab)) = \text{length}_ R(R/(a)) + \text{length}_ R(R/(b))  \]
</div>
  <p> and these lengths are finite. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We saw the finiteness in Lemma <a href="/tag/00PF" data-tag="00PF">10.119.11</a>. Additivity holds since there is a short exact sequence $0 \to R/(a) \to R/(ab) \to R/(b) \to 0$ where the first map is given by multiplication by $b$. (Use length is additive, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00IV" data-tag="00IV">10.52.3</a>.) 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>